event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":79,"item_id":"rs_0aa8b4f023358add016acb0bdfe7dc8194ba4d27ab92de0916","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering code efficiency**\n\nI’m thinking about replacing unique blocks for handlers while inserting constant ranges and local rendering. I notice I’m duplicating edits across whole handlers, and it feels excessive—it’s growing into 140 lines or more! Maybe I should focus on using unique context to expand on duplicates instead. It might help reduce redundancy and streamline the code. I'm curious how that approach could simplify things overall!"}

